                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><div>
<div>
<div>
<div>
<div>
<div>
<div>Minimally invasive surgery has always been the goal and realm pursued in surgical procedures. It has become a clinical skill and concept that modern surgeons must master. To help young physicians and clinical surgical postgraduates better systematically learn this field, we have established the course "Fundamentals and Clinical Practice of Minimally Invasive Surgery." This course covers minimally invasive surgical techniques and developments for common diseases in general surgery, urology, thoracic surgery, obstetrics and gynecology, and pediatrics.</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>
<div>
